<title>USA: N.J. county protests First Union thumbprint policy.</title>
<headline>N.J. county protests First Union thumbprint policy.</headline>
<dateline>ELIZABETH, N.J. 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Union County, N.J., plans to withdraw $15 million from First Union Bank to protest the bank's policy of thumbprinting people who do not hold accounts there and use the bank to cash checks.</p>
<p>Union County Manager Michael Lapolla said the money would be transferred from First Union in stages, with $2 million moved this week.</p>
<p>First Union, based in North Carolina, defended its policy as a deterrent to fraud.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650))</p>
